      "writtenOn": "2017-01-05T19:01:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, I will modify the comment to make it more clear. It is a work around. The reason to fix it here instead of doing it inside the kernel is this bug happens so infrequently and it is caused by concurrency issue of reading the proc fs. The information stored inside proc fs is correct but the read result is corrupted since reading the data is not atomic. So we increased the size of each read to the maximum of proc fs can support and hopefully this will reduce the possibility of having inconsistent read since the frequency of reading the file is reduced to the minimum. And when the inconsistency happens, we will repeatedly read the file until we have a consistent read. And this should be sufficient to fix the problem.",
      "parentUuid": "b7b632e5_8b6d6f75",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 106,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 60
